{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310854,"nonce":"kkGGeuwUQxYeKhwUo0o+wgF5QWU=","title":"NueGraph Stage 1 is COMPLETE, all 8 steps (fee2598c..b53c19c0). Arm A byte-identical end to end on both models; 128-run shadow matrix clean ...","message":"**STAGE 1 IS COMPLETE — all 8 steps landed 2026-08-18..20:**\n`fee2598c` harness · `4e882aa2` NuePlan · `7addbae6` lowered fields + verify ·\n`9d231ef5` attention consumes · `3a752b21` ffn consumes · `1649c8dc` block debug\ngates · `59c29f5a` scaffold deleted · `b53c19c0` docs.\n\n**ACCEPTANCE MET:** arm A (`bench/plan/extract.sh`) BYTE-IDENTICAL from before\nStage 1 to after, both Qwen2.5-0.5B-Q4_K_M and q5_0. Before deleting the verify\nscaffold, the planned route was compared against the live expression on every\nforward across ALL 64 gate combinations x 2 models = **128 runs, zero\nmismatches**. Do that before deleting any future scaffold — it is the only\nmoment the evidence can still be produced.\n\nThe shipped shape and its constraints now live in `nue/ROADMAP.md` (Stage 1) and\n`nue/ARCHITECTURE.md`; the comparison protocol is in `nue/PERFORMANCE.md` under\n*Comparing two trees for identical behaviour*. **Read those, not this note.**\n\nNEXT: Stage 2 (declarative arch descriptors; Mistral first — structure is free,\nIDENTITY is the real work) or the carried-over perf items.\n\nThe original plan is still at `nue/bench/plan/STAGE1_PLAN.md` (43 KB). Read it before\nwriting any Stage 1-adjacent code — it carries the full gate table with default POLARITY,\nthe baseline procedure, 8 landable steps each with its own verify, and a\n\"must not do\" list. Produced 2026-08-18 by an 18-agent workflow (survey → 3\nindependent designs → 3 adversarial judges each → synthesis), 2.9M tokens.\n\n**DESIGN, one line:** compute the per-layer fusion/dispatch route ONCE at build\ntime in `LlamaArch.buildBlock`, lower it to plain `Int` fields on GQAttention /\nSwiGLU / LlamaBlock, and have `forward` read the field instead of re-evaluating\ngates per token. `NuePlan.hx` goes in **`package nue.arch`** beside LlamaArch.\n\n**NINE FLAWS THE JUDGES CAUGHT — each one would have cost a build cycle:**\n1. `new GQAttention`/`new SwiGLU` also happen OUTSIDE LlamaArch\n   (examples/tiny-transformer/Main.hx:148,152; examples/transformer-pieces/Main.hx:34,112),\n   so an unplanned instance must still work ⇒ **0 = unplanned = evaluate live**.\n2. `-1` is unusable as a sentinel: nue has NO non-zero Int initialiser anywhere.\n3. **No `Null\u003cnue-defined-class\u003e` field** — all 7 nullable fields in nue are\n   rayzor-stdlib types. So NO `LlamaModel.plan` field; the plan is a LOCAL.\n4. No new package/directory, and no cross-module static reads (the E0100 family).\n5. `bench/eval/gate.sh --ab` is VACUOUS for this work — same binary, one env var.\n   Compare two TREES instead.\n6. Env pin list had holes; `Sys.getEnvOr` (Sys.hx:65-69) makes an unset `NUE_*`\n   silently inherit its `RAYZOR_*` alias, so aliases must be SCRUBBED.\n7. `[nue-plan]` prefix already belongs to Q4Matmul ⇒ use `[nue-graph]`.\n8. `useFusedMatmul()` prints `[q4-gate]` as a FIRST-READ side effect and\n   LlamaArch does not call it today — so step 1 must avoid calling it or the\n   \"no change\" baseline moves.\n9. A hot-loop rewrite was CUT — it buys nothing with one layer kind and touches\n   an aliased in-place residual (LlamaBlock.hx:99) under a known loop-drop bug.\n\n**THE VERIFICATION IDEA WORTH KEEPING:** `NUE_PLAN_VERIFY` shadow mode — the\nplanner's decision and the live expression BOTH evaluate and are compared on\nevery forward, so equivalence is proven per-call inside ONE binary instead of by\na recompile A/B. Then a 64-run cross-product sweep of the gates. The scaffold is\nDELETED in step 7, so no new gate ships.\n\n**FIRST ACTION IS STEP 1 AND IT IS NOT CODE:** build the harness\n(`nue/bench/plan/pins.sh`, `extract.sh`) and prove it is an ORACLE — run the\nsame HEAD twice with zero changes and require byte-identical extract output.\nExpected on Qwen2.5-0.5B Q4_K_M: `triples fused=2568 split=0`,\n`skipped-dispatcher triple=0 pair=0`, `dispatches=12971`.\n\n**NOT IMPLEMENTED YET.** Related: [[project_nuegraph_stage1_start]] (gate\ninventory), [[project_qwen35_hybrid_ssm_groundwork]] (what Stage 2 must carry).\n\n\n**STEP 1 IS COMPLETE (2026-08-19). BOTH ARMS ARE PROVEN ORACLES.**\n\n| arm | what it pins | proof at a fixed commit |\n|---|---|---|\n| A — generated text + dispatch counters | decode | `extract.sh` output BYTE-IDENTICAL across two runs, both models (`fee2598c`) |\n| B — teacher-forced argmax, `bench/eval` | **prefill** | **top1 = 100.00% over 1530 positions, both models** |\n\nArm B was blocked all along by the release double-free\n([[bugs_release_guard_blind_to_call_shaped_frees]]); with that fixed,\n`bench/eval` scores all 6 chunks and `--dump` produces 1530 rows per model.\nCommands are in `nue/bench/plan/STAGE1_PLAN.md`; run arm B directly, NOT via\n`gate.sh --ab`, which is vacuous for comparing two trees.\n\n**BASELINE CAPTURED** for Qwen2.5-0.5B Q4_K_M and q5_0 — the two models are\ndeliberate: Q4_K_M is pure k-quant so the SPLIT route runs, q5_0 decodes to INT8\nso the FUSED route runs. One model alone cannot tell \"plan preserved\" from \"plan\ndestroyed\".\n\n**NEXT IS STEP 2** — add `NuePlan.hx` in `package nue.arch` (co-located, NOT a\nnew package) and dump the plan under `[nue-graph]`. The acceptance bar is\nunchanged: bit-identical text AND identical dispatch counts before any policy\nchange.\n\n\n**STEP 2 LANDED (`4e882aa2`) AND MEETS THE BAR.** `nue/nue/arch/NuePlan.hx` —\none class, `package nue.arch`, parallel Int arrays for nodes, private opcodes,\nzero mutable statics, built as a LOCAL in `LlamaArch.build()` under the existing\n`NUE_DUMP_Q4_GATES` truthiness and dropped. No field on `LlamaModel`.\n\n| check | Q4_K_M | q5_0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| extract diff | removed=0, added=7, all `[nue-graph]` | removed=0, added=6, all `[nue-graph]` |\n| `dispatches=` | 25434 = 25434 | 25410 = 25410 |\n| `[q4-gate]` lines | 1 = 1 | 1 = 1 |\n| `[output]` | byte-identical | byte-identical |\n| arm B top1 | 100.00% / 1530 | 100.00% / 1530 |\n| flag unset | 0 `[nue-graph]` lines | — |\n\n`decoder_layers` equals `meta.numLayers` and the printed cache kind matches the\n`[kv-cache]` line. `extract.sh` now also captures `[nue-graph]` so later steps\ncan diff the plan itself.\n\n**THE PLAN ALREADY SHOWS SOMETHING:** Qwen2.5-0.5B has TWO layer shapes — 12\nlayers with `v=q8_0` and 12 with `v=int8`. Per-layer weight promotion is real, so\na policy keyed on \"the model's scheme\" would be wrong for half the stack.\n\n**METHOD NOTES.** Capture BEFORE by moving `NuePlan.hx` aside and\n`git checkout`-ing LlamaArch — `git stash push \u003cuntracked\u003e` FAILS silently-ish,\nand the `git stash pop` after it pops an UNRELATED pre-existing stash (that cost\na conflict on `test_results.txt`, which HEAD does not track). No Rust rebuild is\nneeded for a Haxe-only change: same binary, both captures.\n\n**NEXT: STEP 3** — add the lowered `Int` fields (0 = unplanned) plus the\n`NUE_PLAN_VERIFY` shadow scaffold, planner computing while the live expression\nstill executes.\n\n\n**STEP 3 LANDED (`7addbae6`).** Route lowered onto GQAttention/SwiGLU as one Int\nper site (0=unplanned, 1/2 = on/off, 3/4 = the same plus verify). Planner\nwrites; the LIVE expression still decides; under `NUE_PLAN_VERIFY` the two are\ncompared every forward and only reported.\n\n**THE SHADOW MATRIX PASSED: 32 runs, 0 mismatches** — the cross-product of\nNUE_MATMUL x NUE_FUSED_MATMUL x NUE_FUSED_ROWWISE x NUE_FUSED_DISPATCH on both\nmodels. Arm A diff = 0 lines, dispatches unchanged (25434 / 25410); arm B\ntop1 = 100.00% / 1530 on both. 184/184.\n\n**THE TWO EXPRESSIONS MUST NOT BE MERGED** (the plan was right): attention's\n`!useHaxeMat || ...` makes fused TRUE when the Haxe matmul is off and routes to\nthe platform `fusedQkvIntoArr`, while SwiGLU's `useHaxeMat \u0026\u0026 ...` short-circuits\nto the split path. Collapsing them changes the `NUE_MATMUL=0` arm silently.\n\n**PRE-EXISTING, NOT OURS:** `examples/tiny-transformer` exits **139** and\n`examples/transformer-pieces` exits **1** — IDENTICALLY at HEAD with the change\nreverted. They were already broken. The plan cites them as the reason zero must\nmean unplanned; that reasoning still holds, but do not use them as a regression\noracle until they are fixed.\n\n**NEXT: STEP 4** — flip GQAttention to CONSUME the plan (`planHaxeMat != 0`),\nkeeping verify available; then Step 5 does SwiGLU separately so a divergence is\nattributable to one site.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_nuegraph_stage1_plan_ready` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}